{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.105,
            0.127,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "54"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.9,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.139,
            0.902,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "Note that to find d in the AP : 6, 3, 0, – 3, . . ., we have subtracted 6 from 3 and not 3 from 6, i.e., we should subtract the kth term from the (k + 1) th term even if the (k + 1) th term is smaller."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.204,
            0.736,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": "Let us make the concept more clear through some examples."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.239,
            0.901,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "**Example 1 :** For the $\\mathrm{AP}:\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{3}{2}$ , write the first term a and the common difference d."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.309,
            0.545,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Here, $a = \\frac{3}{2}, d = \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{2} = - 1.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.36,
            0.901,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": "the numbers are in AP."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.411,
            0.901,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": "**Example 2 :** Which of the following list of numbers form an AP? If they form an AP, write the next two terms :"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.455,
            0.677,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "(i) 4, 10, 16, 22, . . . (ii) $1,-1,-3,-5,$ . ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.481,
            0.73,
            0.501
          ],
          "content": "(iii) – 2, 2, – 2, 2, – 2, . . . (iv) 1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, . . ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.506,
            0.573,
            0.527
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** (i) We have $a_{2}-a_{1}=10-4=6$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.345,
            0.532,
            0.575,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "a_{3}-a_{2}=16-10=6",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.345,
            0.557,
            0.577,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "a_{4}-a_{3}=22-16=6",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.583,
            0.482,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "i.e., $a _ { { } _ { k \\; + \\; 1 } } - a _ { { } _ { k } }$ is the same every time."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.607,
            0.834,
            0.626
          ],
          "content": "So, the given list of numbers forms an AP with the common difference $d = 6$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.632,
            0.609,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "The next two terms are: $22 + 6 = 28$ and $28+6=34.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.657,
            0.398,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $a_{2}-a_{1}=-1-1=-2$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.679,
            0.532,
            0.7
          ],
          "content": "a_{3}-a_{2}=-3-(-1)=-3+1=-2",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.704,
            0.527,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": "a_{4}-a_{3}=-5-(-3)=-5+3=-2",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.73,
            0.48,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": "i.e., $a _ { { } _ { k \\; + \\; 1 } } - a _ { { } _ { k } }$ is the same every time."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.754,
            0.885,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": "So, the given list of numbers forms an AP with the common difference $d = - 2$ The next two terms are:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.245,
            0.802,
            0.719,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": "-5+(-2)=-7\\qquad and \\qquad-7+(-2)=-9",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.826,
            0.445,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $a_{2}-a_{1}=2-(-2)=2+2=4$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.851,
            0.375,
            0.871
          ],
          "content": "a_{3}-a_{2}=-2-2=-4",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.873,
            0.764,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": "As $a_{_2}-a_{_1}\\ne a_{_3}-a_{_2}$ , the given list of numbers does not form an AP."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.966,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
